  SECURITY REPORT — Score: 70/100 [MEDIUM]
  The codebase has several high-risk vulnerabilities, primarily related to authentication gaps, hardcoded secrets, and mass assignment issues. Immediate attention is required to secure the application before deployment.

  Findings (7):
  [HIGH    ] HardcodedSecret in app/utils/auth.py
             The SECRET_KEY is hardcoded as 'changeme-dev-secret', which is insecure.
             Fix: Use a strong, randomly generated secret key and ensure it is set via environment variables.
  [HIGH    ] AuthenticationGap in app/routes/user_routes.py
             The endpoint '/users' does not require authentication.
             Fix: Add Depends(oauth2_scheme) to the get_users function to require authentication.
  [HIGH    ] MassAssignment in app/routes/user_routes.py
             The UserCreate schema exposes the password field directly, which can lead to mass assignment vulnerabilities.
             Fix: Ensure that the password is hashed before being assigned to the User model.
  [MEDIUM  ] CORSIssue in app/main.py
             CORS is set to allow all origins, which is too permissive for production.
             Fix: Restrict allow_origins to a specific list of trusted domains.
  [MEDIUM  ] MissingValidation in app/schemas/user.py
             The username and password fields do not have maximum length validation.
             Fix: Add max_length constraints to the username and password fields in the UserCreate schema.
  [MEDIUM  ] WeakJWT in app/utils/auth.py
             The JWT secret key is weak and the tokens do not have an expiry set.
             Fix: Use a strong secret key and ensure that tokens have a reasonable expiry time.
  [MEDIUM  ] RateLimiting in app/routes/auth_routes.py
             There is no rate limiting implemented for the login and signup endpoints.
             Fix: Implement rate limiting to prevent brute-force attacks on these endpoints.

  Passed: No SQL injection found, Passwords properly hashed with bcrypt
