  SECURITY REPORT — Score: 70/100 [MEDIUM]
  The codebase has several critical authentication gaps and mass assignment vulnerabilities that need to be addressed before deployment. Additionally, there are issues with CORS configuration and input validation that could expose sensitive user data.

  Findings (6):
  [HIGH    ] AuthenticationGap in app/routes/comment_routes.py
             GET /comments/{id} does not require authentication, allowing unauthenticated users to access comments.
             Fix: Add Depends(get_current_user) to the get_comment function.
  [HIGH    ] AuthenticationGap in app/routes/post_routes.py
             GET /posts/{id} does not require authentication, allowing unauthenticated users to access posts.
             Fix: Add Depends(get_current_user) to the get_post function.
  [HIGH    ] MassAssignment in app/models/users.py
             User model exposes fields like password directly, which could lead to mass assignment vulnerabilities.
             Fix: Use Pydantic models to control which fields can be set during user creation and updates.
  [HIGH    ] PasswordExposure in app/routes/user_routes.py
             GET /users/{id} returns user object which may expose sensitive information.
             Fix: Exclude sensitive fields like password from the UserResponse model.
  [MEDIUM  ] CORSIssue in app/main.py
             CORS is set to allow all origins, which is insecure for production.
             Fix: Restrict allow_origins to a specific list of trusted domains.
  [MEDIUM  ] MissingValidation in app/schemas/user.py
             UserCreate schema does not limit the length of username and password fields.
             Fix: Add max_length to username and password fields in UserCreate schema.

  Passed: No SQL injection found, Passwords properly hashed with bcrypt
