  SECURITY REPORT — Score: 70/100 [MEDIUM]
  The codebase has several security vulnerabilities, particularly around authentication and configuration management. Immediate attention is needed to enforce authentication on key endpoints and to secure sensitive configurations.

  Findings (6):
  [HIGH    ] AuthenticationGap in app/routes/contact_routes.py
             Endpoints for managing contacts do not require authentication.
             Fix: Add `Depends(get_current_user)` to each endpoint to enforce authentication.
  [MEDIUM  ] HardcodedSecret in app/utils/auth.py
             The SECRET_KEY is hardcoded as 'changeme-dev-secret'.
             Fix: Use an environment variable for SECRET_KEY and ensure it is not a weak value.
  [MEDIUM  ] MassAssignment in app/routes/contact_routes.py
             Contact creation and update endpoints allow mass assignment of fields.
             Fix: Use Pydantic's `exclude_unset` or explicitly define allowed fields in the schemas.
  [MEDIUM  ] CORSIssue in app/main.py
             CORS is set to allow all origins, which is insecure for production.
             Fix: Restrict `allow_origins` to specific domains in production.
  [MEDIUM  ] WeakJWT in app/utils/auth.py
             The JWT does not have an expiry set in the token creation.
             Fix: Ensure tokens have a reasonable expiration time.
  [MEDIUM  ] MissingValidation in app/schemas/contact.py
             String fields in schemas do not have length limits.
             Fix: Add `max_length` to string fields in Pydantic models.

  Passed: No SQL injection found, Passwords properly hashed with bcrypt
