  SECURITY REPORT — Score: 70/100 [MEDIUM]
  The codebase has several security vulnerabilities, particularly in CORS configuration and weak JWT secret management. Authentication gaps and mass assignment risks are present, which could lead to unauthorized access and data exposure.

  Findings (5):
  [HIGH    ] CORSIssue in app/main.py
             CORS is set to allow all origins, which can expose the API to cross-origin attacks.
             Fix: Restrict allow_origins to a specific list of trusted domains.
  [HIGH    ] WeakJWT in app/utils/auth.py
             The SECRET_KEY is set to a weak default value ('changeme-dev-secret').
             Fix: Use a strong, randomly generated secret key stored in environment variables.
  [MEDIUM  ] AuthenticationGap in app/routes/task_routes.py
             GET /tasks/{id} does not require authentication, exposing task details to unauthenticated users.
             Fix: Add Depends(get_current_user) to the get_task function to enforce authentication.
  [MEDIUM  ] MassAssignment in app/routes/task_routes.py
             The update_task function allows mass assignment of fields, potentially exposing sensitive fields.
             Fix: Use Pydantic's `exclude` or `exclude_unset` to prevent mass assignment of sensitive fields.
  [MEDIUM  ] MissingValidation in app/schemas/user.py
