  The codebase has several security vulnerabilities, particularly around hardcoded secrets and mass assignment. CORS settings are too permissive, and there are missing validations that could lead to insecure direct object references. Immediate attention is needed to address these issues before deployment.

  Findings (6):
  [HIGH    ] HardcodedSecret in app/routes/seed_routes.py
             Hardcoded passwords in the seed data.
             Fix: Use environment variables or a secure vault to manage sensitive data.
  [HIGH    ] MassAssignment in app/routes/user_routes.py
             User creation allows mass assignment of fields, including password.
             Fix: Use Pydantic's `exclude` or `include` to limit fields that can be set.
  [MEDIUM  ] CORSIssue in app/main.py
             CORS is set to allow all origins, which is insecure for production.
             Fix: Restrict `allow_origins` to trusted domains only.
  [MEDIUM  ] MissingValidation in app/models/users.py
             String fields (username, password) lack length limits.
             Fix: Add `max_length` to string fields in the User model.
  [MEDIUM  ] IDOR in app/routes/comment_routes.py
             GET /comments/{id} does not verify if the comment belongs to the current user.
             Fix: Check if `comment.user_id == current_user.id` before returning the comment.
  [MEDIUM  ] IDOR in app/routes/post_routes.py
             GET /posts/{id} does not verify if the post belongs to the current user.
